{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793742864,"nonce":"wawHkUJkg3smDKh9u30Qmj/TprM=","title":"Enforce landing-demo compute and relay budgets","message":"Implement resource limits for anonymous demo leases separately from paid synced workspaces: CPU/memory, compiler concurrency, runtime/idle expiry, retained disk bytes, preview process count, transfer size and request rates. Proposed pilot policy is 5 minute idle expiry and a 15 minute maximum lease, subject to measured usability; no background timer or signed-out browser may perpetually renew a lease. Do not change paid workspace expiry defaults to these demo settings.\n\nThe editor and initial cached app remain usable while compute is queued or unavailable. Keep real progress/error/retry feedback. Stop or release session work when the visitor leaves and reap abandoned compute server-side. Reuse only clean immutable templates/artifacts. Audit the DO relay's upstream WebSocket/event lifetime before assuming duration hibernation, and avoid resource polls while the sidebar is hidden. Record per-session CPU seconds, peak/resident RAM, storage, build count, Worker/DO requests and active duration, and actual bytes served.\n\nDone when a bounded load/abuse test cannot exceed host admission/compiler/storage quotas, all failed/expired leases are cleaned, and a measured host-capacity/cost estimate is published here. No purchase or production-scale concurrency is implied by the current NUC pilot.\n\nPart of landing deployment: git-bug 56b531e22a0bf22913529f321d5b0f7d3ab02bef3d18192d73838675fff95704","files":null}]}